# 2026-07-29: murata_l072 firmware intermediates. The 35 .o + 34 .d files under
# build/ were tracked by accident and dirtied 31 files on every `mingw32-make`,
# making `git status` useless for spotting real changes. The FLASHABLE artifacts
# (firmware.bin/.hex/.elf/.map) stay tracked deliberately — they let someone
# flash a board without the arm-none-eabi toolchain, and the .map catches size
# regressions.
LifeTrac-v25/DESIGN-CONTROLLER/firmware/murata_l072/build/**/*.o
LifeTrac-v25/DESIGN-CONTROLLER/firmware/murata_l072/build/**/*.d
LifeTrac-v25/DESIGN-CONTROLLER/firmware/murata_l072/build/firmware.ld
LifeTrac-v25/DESIGN-CONTROLLER/firmware/murata_l072/build/*.preproc
# Host-side bench test binaries built by the `make check-*` targets.
LifeTrac-v25/DESIGN-CONTROLLER/firmware/murata_l072/build/*.exe

# 2026-08-16: repo-root bench scratch. The radio campaign leaves per-run
# transcripts and probe dumps at the repo root (`_rs115_*.log`,
# `_saturation_run*.log`, `_run*_summary.txt`, `_fwbuild*.log`, …) — ~130 of
# them by now. They are working notes, not evidence: anything load-bearing is
# archived under DESIGN-CONTROLLER/bench-evidence/ with its SHA. Left
# untracked they are one `git add -A` away from landing in a commit and
# burying the real diff, which is why they are pinned here rather than swept
# away — the files stay on disk, they just stop being offered.
# Anchored to the root so nested `_`-prefixed sources are unaffected.
/_*
/run_tests_full.log
# Stray root copy of the helper-dir OpenOCD cfg (byte-identical to
# firmware/x8_lora_bootloader_helper/09_resume_h7.cfg; that one is canonical).
/09_resume_h7.cfg
